	(text "MEGA-KVM keyboard sub-board (issue 0045 round 6). Two per Mimas, one beside each long side,\nunder the shield overhang beside the Mimas, on its own 3 mm standoffs.\n\n* J5-style 2x5 box headers (MEGA65 keyboard pinout: 1 GND, 2 3.3 V from the DUT (sense),\n  3-7 n.c., 8 KIO8, 9 KIO9, 10 KIO10), each directly below its DUT's JB1 on the shield.\n* 47 ohm series on KIO8/9/10, 10 k on the 3.3 V sense (100 k pull-down on the shield).\n* 2x6 male header to a 2x6 11 mm socket on the shield's underside; the sub-board sits 2.5 mm\n  lower than the Mimas (3 mm vs 5.5 mm standoffs) so the JB1 pin tails clear the J5 bodies.\n  One identical board on both sides (translated, not mirrored). Slot A = lower Mimas y. P12 side: A = DUT0, B = DUT3; P13 side: A = DUT2, B = DUT1.\n\nGenerated by ../scripts/gen_sch.py from ../scripts/design.py -- edit those and regenerate."
